Default: Executive and professional.

# PART 8 — FACTUAL INTEGRITY AND CLAIM VERIFICATION

This section is NON-NEGOTIABLE.

Create a claim verification layer.

Every professional claim in the generated resume and cover letter must have traceable supporting evidence.

For each claim, maintain:

- Claim text.
- Source profile field.
- Original source text.
- Source employment role.
- Verification status.
- Whether the wording was modified by AI.

Use three verification states:

<VERIFIED>
Supported by the master resume or user-confirmed information.

<NEEDS CONFIRMATION>
Potentially true, but not adequately supported.

<UNSUPPORTED>
No evidence exists.

Only VERIFIED claims may appear automatically in the final resume and cover letter.

NEEDS CONFIRMATION claims must be presented to the user for approval.

UNSUPPORTED claims must not be included.

Examples:

Job requirement: Experience with Salesforce.

Master resume: No Salesforce experience.

Correct AI behaviour:
"Salesforce experience is not documented in your master resume. Have you used Salesforce professionally?"

Incorrect AI behaviour:
Add Salesforce to the skills section automatically.

Additional safeguards:

- Never invent numbers.
- Never invent years of experience.
- Never upgrade job titles.
- Never imply team leadership without supporting evidence.
- Never claim direct ownership when the user only supported a project.
- Never convert participation into project leadership.
- Never invent company-specific experience.

The AI must preserve the distinction between managed, led, supported, coordinated, contributed and participated.

